Is that official?

[/quote]

No. But I do not see much room for debate here.&nbsp; I think too much is being made of the word &quot;until&quot;. They used &quot;until&quot; because the effect has to persist for an entire round after her turn ends. Mistbound does not say &quot;until the end of your Start of Turn Phase&quot;, which is what some of you seem to want it to say. Your Start Of Turn Phase does not have little mini start/end points inside it, thats a <em>bit</em> much in my opinion. It is much cleaner to say they both trigger at the Start of Turn and resolve them like any other simultaneous effect.

[quote="phantaskippy"]

There is a difference between the time a card enters play and the time it activates, I think it could be possible that there could be an effect that ends right before the start of turn.There is timing inside of the start of your turn. &nbsp;Your start of turn ends after the previous turns end of turn ends. &nbsp;Multiple effects can resolve during your start of turn, and then it ends when it is time for your Play a Card action.Again the correct definition of Until would not include any of your start of turn. &nbsp;It may be clear to you, but definitionally the effect should end before your turn starts. &nbsp;I&#39;m not going to assume that &gt;G is using the less correct interpretation.

[/quote]

But until you actually&nbsp;<em>get</em> to your Start of turn Phase, the trigger is not met. I highly doubt the intent is &quot;right before the start of your turn, destroy this card&quot; you know?&nbsp;

&quot;start of turn&quot; is a sub-sect of your turn, it does not get broken up into smaller sub-sects. The Start of Turn phase ends before you start resolving effects. For Villains that flip at the start of turn, like the Rat, you don&#39;t flip him (due to SoT effect) then procceed to resolve the SoT effect on his flip side. Why? Because the SoT phase had already come and gone and you are just resolving the effects that triggered as a result of hitting SoT.&nbsp;

So the &quot;until&quot; wording really reads &quot;Until you get to the start of your turn phase...&quot; not &quot;right before you get to the start of your turn phase&quot;. The latter is a very wonky interpretation of how phases work in this game. Nothing else works that way.

